# Competency question: "What are the first-class object kinds of the study & data-design
# vocabulary?" Exercises the STATISTICS-charter "Study and data" surface: over a worked survey
# scene the reasoning-free query reads back the asserted kind of each object making up the
# design — the target-of-inference and measurement spine (population, frame, sample, unit,
# variable), the variable metadata (role, scale, unit policy, missing-value code, missingness
# indicator/mechanism), and the design apparatus (sampling weight, stratum, cluster, survey
# design, data transformation, derived variable). Scoped so items are fixture-local and kinds
# are math:. Over the fixture the answer is exactly the seventeen study & data-design classes.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>

SELECT ?item ?kind WHERE {
    ?item a ?kind .
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?item), "http://example.org/math/"))
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?kind), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/"))
}
ORDER BY ?item
